## Expected package.json scripts

Generated add-if-missing by `bootstrap-project.mjs` (a project may already define
its own bodies — these are the meta-govern defaults). `typecheck` is added only
for TypeScript stacks and, when present, folded into `validate`/`validate:fast`.

- `dev` — local dev server
- `quality:check` — full deterministic quality scan (`quality-checks/index.mjs`)
- `quality:check:staged` — staged-only scan (`--scope staged --fail-level high`)
- `size-guard` — file-size-growth-guard
- `typecheck` — type-check, no emit (TS stacks only)
- `test` — the project's test runner
- `validate` — `quality:check && size-guard [&& typecheck] && test && mark-validate-pass.mjs` (the LAST step writes the Stop-gate success sentinel)
- `validate:fast` — `quality:check [&& typecheck]` (no size-guard / tests)
- `docs:index` — régénère `docs/index.html` (make-index)
- `docs-map:check` — valide `docs/docs-map.json`
- `docs:check` — no-markdown-guard (aucun `.md` sous `docs/`)
- `predeploy` — predeploy-check (compensation locale de CI serveur quand `ciPolicy = local-compensation`)

## Expected `.husky/pre-commit`

Gate runs on STAGED/changed code only, via `node` (scripts are `.mjs`, not pm
sub-commands):

```bash
node .claude/scripts/file-size-growth-guard.mjs
node .claude/scripts/quality-checks/index.mjs --scope staged --fail-level high
node .claude/scripts/docs-html/no-markdown-guard.mjs
node .claude/scripts/check-docs-map.mjs
```

Compensation CI locale (quand `ciPolicy = local-compensation` dans `.claude/.meta-govern.json`) :
en l'absence de CI serveur, la couverture tient sur deux briques locales — `predeploy-check.mjs`
(scan complet avant tout déploiement, lancé via `npm run predeploy`) et le gate Stop durci
(`enforce-workflow.mjs` sous `MG_HEADLESS_RUN=1`, qui exige `validate` inconditionnellement sur
les runs autonomes). audit-project présente alors le CI serveur en OPTION, non en manquement.

